Just to clarify (for those readers with even less experience than me,
which is "not many"):

For most adventurers, it's 1/2 or 3/8 (1/2 minus 25% of 1/2). You'll
get the 3/8 randomly 1 out of 4 times you offer to sell an unidentified
object.

So a $200 object might get an offer of $100 or $75, and an $80
object might get an offer of $40 or $30. (That latter one is what
makes $80 scrolls look like $60 if you don't ask again to be sure.)

For some adventurers (like lower-level tourists, or if the shopkeeper
can see a shirt on you), it's 1/3 or 3/12 (1/3 minus 25% of 1/3). Again,
the 3/12 will be random.

